  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Studio Tamani 2015-2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Studio Tamani 2015-2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Contribute to peace in Mali and to reconciliation and dialogue between all sectors of the population2) Promote professionalization of the Malian media sector through an original media platform with a network of professional journalists throughout the country.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att &#xf6;ka tillg&#xe5;ngen till opartiska nyheter och information i hela landet och att d&#xe4;rigenom st&#xe4;rka yttrandefrihet och ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande, samt f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra demokratiskt beslutsfattande. Genom att &#xf6;ka f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else och kunskap avser insatsen bidra till fred, f&#xf6;rsoning och dialog. Detta ska ske genom att dagligen producera nyheter och debattprogram, som s&#xe4;nds genom ett n&#xe4;tverk av oberoende radiokanaler. Studio Tamani &#xe4;r &#xe4;ven aktiva p&#xe5; Twitter och l&#xe4;gger ut alla debattprogram p&#xe5; Youtube. Under projektperioden &#xe4;r ambitionen att &#xe4;ven ut&#xf6;ka s&#xe4;ndningen till TV och genom mobiltelefonl&#xf6;sningar. Studio Tamani har 30 anst&#xe4;llda journalister, som f&#xe5;r kontinuerlig utbildning och st&#xf6;d i syfte att st&#xe4;rka deras professionella kapacitet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution aims to increase the access to impartial news and information throughout the country, thereby strengthening freedom of speech and accountability, and improving democratic decision-making. Through increasing understanding and knowledge the contribution strives to contribute to peace, reconciliation and dialogue. This will be ensured through the daily production of news and debate programs, which are broadcast through a network of independent radios. Studio Tamani are also active on Twitter and post all debate programs on Youtube. During the project period, the aim is to increase the broadcasting to TV and mobile telephone solutions. Studio Tamani has 30 employed journalists, who receive continous training and support in order to strengthen their professional capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
